<title> Monoarticular Arthritis: Diagnosis.</title>
<graphic href="eee0702-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Pain or swelling in a single joint. Perform history and physical examination</label>
<path target="cell-3"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Significant trauma or focal bone pain?</label>
<path target="cell-5">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-4">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-4">
<label>Effusion or signs of inflammation?</label>
<path target="cell-6">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-7">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-6">
<label>Joint aspiration.</label>
<path target="cell-8">Unsuccessful aspiration</path>
<path target="cell-9">Successful aspiration</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-8">
<label>Probable inflammatory process. Re-evaluate.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-9">
<label>Bloody?</label>
<path target="cell-13">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-10">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-13">
<label>Consider coagulopathy, trauma, pigmented villonodular synovitis, tumor, charcot joint, pseudogout.</label>
<path target="cell-14"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-14">
<label>Check prothrombin time&#x002F;partial thromboplastin time, platelet count, bleeding time; obtain radiograph and, if negative, MRI.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-10">
<label>Fat or other bone marrow elements?</label>
<path target="cell-15">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-11">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-15">
<label>Consider intra-articular fracture; obtain radiograph, MRI if negative.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-11">
<label>Synovial fluid contains &#x003E;2000 WBC?</label>
<path target="cell-16">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-17">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-16">
<label>Crystals identified.</label>
<path target="cell-18">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-19">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-18">
<label>Suspect monosodium urate (gout) or calcium pyrophosphate dihydrate (pseudogout).</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-19">
<label>Positive synovial culture or Gram stain, or positive urethral, pharyngeal, rectal cultures when gonococcal arthritis is suspected?</label>
<path target="cell-20">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-21">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-20">
<label>Infectious (septic) arthritis.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-21">
<label>If sterile inflammatory joint fluid, suspect spondyloarthritis, RA, SLE, sarcoidosis, Lyme disease, or mycobacterial or fungal infection in the appropriate clinical setting.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-17">
<label>Osteoarthritis, internal derangement, soft tissue injury, viral infection.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-7">
<label>Tenderness at tendons or bursae.</label>
<path target="cell-23">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-100">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-23">
<label>Bursitis or tendonitis.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-100">
<label>Consider radiograph and clinical follow-up.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-5">
<label>Radiograph.</label>
<path target="cell-24">Abnormal</path>
<path target="cell-4">Normal</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-24">
<label>Fracture or metabolic bone disease.</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>RA, rheumatoid arthritis; SLE, systemic lupus erythematosus; MRI, magnetic resonance imaging. Adapted from American College of Rheumatology Ad Hoc Guidelines. Guidelines for acute musculoskeletal symptoms. <em>Arthritis Rheum</em> 196;<strong>39</strong>:1-8.<xref ref="pubmed8546717" resource="acc015" />
</footnote>
</footnotes>
